WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.076
This is the EnMD Digital Platform,
from the Energy Management

2
00:00:07.076 --> 00:00:11.979
Division of the National Cleaner
Production Centre, Sri Lanka.

3
00:00:12.329 --> 00:00:15.794
Every energy audit tool the
division uses, in

4
00:00:15.794 --> 00:00:19.562
one website, on your
computer, tablet or phone.

5
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:26.477
Open it in any browser. On a phone, the
same pages fit the small screen.

6
00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:32.165
Press Get started, and type the
four digit access code. It

7
00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:36.802
is asked once each time you open the
platform in a browser tab.

8
00:00:37.152 --> 00:00:40.095
Each tool then asks for
its own app code,

9
00:00:40.095 --> 00:00:43.403
once each time you open it
in a browser tab.

10
00:00:44.967 --> 00:00:48.274
The dashboard shows seven tools
as coloured tiles.

11
00:00:48.624 --> 00:00:53.595
Type in the search box to find one
quickly, and tap a tile to open it.

12
00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:58.121
First, LuxLog, the
lighting survey app.

13
00:00:58.471 --> 00:01:01.539
It opens with an example
hospital survey, so

14
00:01:01.539 --> 00:01:05.106
you can try every tool before
you start your own.

15
00:01:05.456 --> 00:01:09.968
On the Project tab, type the site, the
survey date, who surveyed,

16
00:01:09.968 --> 00:01:14.907
and the lux meter used. Press Start my
own survey when you are ready.

17
00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:20.905
Each area you survey is a section, with
its own sketch and readings.

18
00:01:21.255 --> 00:01:26.866
LuxLog reads the section name and
picks the room type,

19
00:01:26.866 --> 00:01:32.686
here Kitchen, with its JIS Z9110
range of 300 to 750 lux

20
00:01:32.686 --> 00:01:39.175
and the OSHA minimum. You can also
choose from 33 room types.

21
00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:45.191
Sketch the room with walls, doors and
windows, and place furniture,

22
00:01:45.191 --> 00:01:49.267
light fittings, fans and air
conditioners from the symbols.

23
00:01:49.617 --> 00:01:54.247
On an Android phone, the camera room
scan measures the room as

24
00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:59.025
you tap each corner, and finds tables,
chairs, beds and screens.

25
00:01:59.025 --> 00:02:04.402
On an iPhone or a computer, type the room
size or draw it on the grid.

26
00:02:04.752 --> 00:02:09.766
The camera works only on your phone. No
photos or video are uploaded.

27
00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:14.426
Tap where you measured and
type the lux from your

28
00:02:14.426 --> 00:02:17.893
meter, or press Auto spots to
place a grid of spots.

29
00:02:18.243 --> 00:02:21.509
Mark an area, such as the
cooking area, and the

30
00:02:21.509 --> 00:02:24.857
spots inside it get that
area's own lux level.

31
00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:31.275
Every reading is rated at once: Low,
Good or High against the

32
00:02:31.275 --> 00:02:36.619
JIS range, and checked against the
OSHA minimum as Pass or Below.

33
00:02:36.969 --> 00:02:41.653
The panel shows the average, minimum,
maximum and uniformity, and

34
00:02:41.653 --> 00:02:46.847
the measurement log lists every reading,
which you can open or delete.

35
00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.688
The lux map shades the drawing
between your spots,

36
00:02:51.688 --> 00:02:54.929
so dark and bright areas
stand out at a glance.

37
00:02:55.279 --> 00:02:58.425
In the 3D tab, turn the room,
walk through it,

38
00:02:58.425 --> 00:03:01.722
and choose the view that goes
into the report.

39
00:03:03.267 --> 00:03:07.939
The Report tab sums up every
section against the JIS range.

40
00:03:08.289 --> 00:03:14.635
The Word report has the summary chart and,
for each section, the sketch,

41
00:03:14.635 --> 00:03:20.452
a 3D view, and a table of every spot
with its JIS and OSHA result.

42
00:03:20.452 --> 00:03:27.213
There is also an Excel workbook, and
drawings export as SVG or AutoCAD DXF.

43
00:03:27.563 --> 00:03:31.224
Your survey saves on the device
as you work. Download

44
00:03:31.224 --> 00:03:34.966
a backup to carry on with
another phone or computer.

45
00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:41.995
Next, the calculators. The solar,
compressor, boiler, air conditioning and

46
00:03:41.995 --> 00:03:48.383
ESO tools are built from the division's own
Excel workbooks, with the same formulas.

47
00:03:48.733 --> 00:03:54.537
Change a highlighted box, and every result,
chart and check updates straight away.

48
00:03:54.887 --> 00:03:59.340
The calculations were checked against
LibreOffice with many random

49
00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:04.146
sets of inputs, and your values are
saved on this device as you work.

50
00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:10.632
Inputs that matter most carry an orange
Critical badge. A ten percent

51
00:04:10.632 --> 00:04:15.429
change in one of them moves a key
result by five percent or more.

52
00:04:15.779 --> 00:04:20.238
Tap the badge to see which result it
changes, and by how much.

53
00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:24.838
The checks panel shows the
workbook's own model

54
00:04:24.838 --> 00:04:28.350
checks. A green tick means
everything is consistent.

55
00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:33.698
When you finish, use the Download
group at the top right.

56
00:04:34.048 --> 00:04:38.310
Word makes a complete report, with a
cover page, summary, your

57
00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:42.859
inputs, every result, the checks,
charts and a sign-off section.

58
00:04:43.209 --> 00:04:47.349
Excel gives back the filled
workbook, with all its formulas.

59
00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:53.286
The rooftop solar tool sizes the
system from the roof and the

60
00:04:53.286 --> 00:04:58.181
district, with sunshine data calibrated
to the Global Solar Atlas.

61
00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:02.074
It builds a cash flow of up to
30 years, with net

62
00:05:02.074 --> 00:05:05.913
present value, payback, and
seventeen model checks.

63
00:05:07.467 --> 00:05:11.659
The sub-meter tool checks site meters
against a reference logger.

64
00:05:11.659 --> 00:05:15.809
The units and the error of every
meter are worked out for you.

65
00:05:16.159 --> 00:05:19.967
Add photos and a signature, and
the Word report comes

66
00:05:19.967 --> 00:05:24.501
out in the division's template,
exactly like the Excel macro.

67
00:05:26.067 --> 00:05:30.474
The Smart ESO Sheet lists every
energy saving opportunity,

68
00:05:30.474 --> 00:05:34.195
one row per measure, just
like the Excel sheet.

69
00:05:34.545 --> 00:05:39.795
Cost and greenhouse gas savings use
current prices and IPCC

70
00:05:39.795 --> 00:05:45.639
2006 factors, and the Word export
matches the sheet's own table.

71
00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:51.429
The compressor tool compares the
existing machine with a new one

72
00:05:51.429 --> 00:05:56.139
at the same air demand, with pressure
correction and part load power.

73
00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:02.369
The boiler tool finds the efficiency by
the indirect heat loss method,

74
00:06:02.369 --> 00:06:07.855
and assesses five measures, with their
interaction and a safe stack temperature.

75
00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:13.771
The air conditioning tool compares
six system types against

76
00:06:13.771 --> 00:06:18.958
the existing non inverter units, in
energy, cost and carbon dioxide.

77
00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:24.241
Your work stays on your device.
In the sub-meter tool,

78
00:06:24.241 --> 00:06:27.925
Backup and Restore move an
audit to another device.

79
00:06:29.567 --> 00:06:33.672
The EnMD Digital Platform.
Developed by Vihindu

80
00:06:33.672 --> 00:06:38.015
Jayawardena, for the Energy
Management Division.

81
00:06:38.365 --> 00:06:40.350
Choose a tool, and
begin.
